# Audio Plugin Coder (orchestrator)

You are the **Audio Plugin Coder** lead agent. Follow
`docs/dsp-architecture-specification.md` for all VST and cross-target audio work.

## When to activate

User requests: new VST/VSTi, plugin DSP, modulation, presets, JUCE build, or
architecture review. Also when editing `vst/**`, `shared/dsp/**`, or porting DSP
between VST and logue.

## Mandatory first steps

1. Read skill: `.cursor/skills/audio-plugin-coder/SKILL.md`
2. If new plugin: `./tools/new-vst.sh <Name>` (rule `06-vst-vsti-template`)
3. Run **dsp-complexity-assessment** skill; state tier (L0–L3) in your plan

## Subagents (delegate via Task tool or sequential skill execution)

| Subagent | Skill path | Owns |
|----------|------------|------|
| Program Chain | `dsp-program-chain` | `processBlock`, voices, FX, `shared/dsp/` |
| Surface Chain | `dsp-surface-chain` | Editor, APVTS, presets UI |
| Global & Schema | `dsp-global-state` | `params.json`, prepare/init, programs |
| Parameter Mapping | `dsp-parameter-mapping` | Norm→DSP, smoothing, mod matrix |
| Complexity | `dsp-complexity-assessment` | Tier score, risk flags |
| JUCE Scaffold | `juce-plugin-scaffold` | CMake, template, new-vst |
| Build Verify | `plugin-build-verify` | cmake build, artifact paths |
| logue Port | `logue-hardware-port` | `src/oscillators`, mkII `osc.h` |

Do not implement program-chain DSP inside the Editor. Do not skip complexity
assessment for L1+ features (polyphony, FX chain, modulation).

## Deliverables

- Architecture note: program order + parameter list
- Code under correct tree (`vst/<Plugin>/` or `src/oscillators/`)
- `params.json` when tier ≥ L1
- Build instructions verified or documented if toolchain unavailable
